s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:3:\"7.2\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:3;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:11:\"development\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:4;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:7:\"release\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:35:\"https://wordpress.org/news/?p=22019\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:364:\"The first Release Candidate (“RC1”) for WordPress 7.2 is ready for download and testing! This version of the WordPress software is still under development. Please do not install, run, or test this version of WordPress on production or mission-critical websites. Instead, it’s recommended to evaluate RC1 on a test server and site. WordPress 7.2 RC1 [&#8230;]\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"David Baumwald\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:10144:\"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The first Release Candidate (“RC1”) for WordPress 7.2 is ready for download and testing!</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>This version of the WordPress software is still under development</strong>. Please do not install, run, or test this version of WordPress on production or mission-critical websites. Instead, it’s recommended to evaluate RC1 on a test server and site.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress 7.2 RC1 can be tested using any of the following methods:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Plugin</strong></td><td>Install and activate the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/wordpress-beta-tester/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">WordPress Beta Tester</a> plugin on a WordPress install. (Select the “Bleeding edge” channel and “Beta/RC Only” stream.)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Direct Download</strong></td><td>Download the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/wordpress-7.2-RC1.zip\">RC1 version (zip)</a> and install it on a WordPress website.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Command Line</strong></td><td>Use this <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/cli/\">WP-CLI</a> command: <br><code>wp core update --version=7.2-RC1</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>WordPress Playground</strong></td><td>Use the <a href=\"http://playground.wordpress.net/release\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">WordPress Playground instance</a> to test the software directly in your browser.  No setup required – just click and go!</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The scheduled final release date for WordPress 7.2 is <strong>December 8, 2026</strong>. The full <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/core/2026/10/06/wordpress-7-2-release-party-schedule/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">release schedule can be found here</a>. Your help testing Beta and RC versions is vital to making this release as stable and powerful as possible. Thank you to everyone who contributes by testing!</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Please continue checking the <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/core/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Make WordPress Core blog</a> for <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/core/tag/7-2\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">7.2-related posts</a> in the coming weeks for more information.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Core Changes Since Beta 5</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/news/2026/10/wordpress-7-2-beta-1-is-ready-for-download-and-testing/\">Beta 1 announcement</a> for details on WordPress 7.2.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can browse the technical details for all issues addressed since Beta 5 using these links:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/query?changetime=11%2F10%2F2026..11%2F17%2F2026&amp;milestone=7.2&amp;status=closed&amp;group=component&amp;order=id&amp;col=id&amp;col=milestone&amp;col=owner&amp;col=type&amp;col=priority\">Closed 7.2 WordPress Core Trac tickets</a> since November 10, 2026</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/commits/wp/7.2?since=2026-11-10&amp;until=2026-11-17\">7.2 Gutenberg commits</a> since November 10, 2026</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress 7.2 Release Candidate 1 brings additional bug fixes, accessibility improvements, and compatibility updates as the release moves closer to its December 8 launch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Recent refinements include fixes to client-side media uploads, improvements to the new random-content redirect feature, and better keyboard navigation through a skip link in the WordPress admin bar. Additional updates improve plugin dependency messaging, script module translations, and the reliability of the HTML and Interactivity APIs.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Developers will also benefit from continued Abilities API refinements and updates to bundled libraries, including PHPMailer, Requests, getID3, and sodium_compat.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/66490\">Trac #66490</a>, <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/66681\">Trac #66681</a>, <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/66625\">Trac #66625</a>, <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/66331\">Trac #66331</a>, <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/66591\">Trac #66591</a>, <a href=\"https://core.trac.wordpress.org/ticket/65984\">Trac #65984</a></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Additional Block Editor Improvements</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress 7.2 RC1 includes further refinements to the block editor, addressing issues with duplicated block content, keyboard interactions on iOS, and revision previews. Improvements to the Interactivity API prevent outdated navigation responses from replacing newer content, while additional fixes improve plugin installation workflows, featured image compatibility, and link suggestions. The transition to modern SVG icons also continues throughout WordPress administration.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/pull/86839\">GitHub #86839</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/pull/86703\">GitHub #86703</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/pull/86608\">GitHub #86608</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/pull/78367\">GitHub #78367</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/pull/86854\">GitHub #86854</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Want to know more about this release? Here are some highlights:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>New Ipsum default theme</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Expanded responsive design and Gallery controls</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improved Global Styles and typography tools</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enhanced Canvas Notes and collaboration</li>\n\n\n\n<li>New DataForm block settings inspector</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Faster media uploads and image processing</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Modernized WordPress admin with SVG icons</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Faster admin navigation and asset loading</li>\n\n\n\n<li>New “On This Day” widget and random post discovery</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improved translation update management</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accessibility, security, and PHP 8.6 compatibility improvements</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How you can contribute</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress is open source software made possible by a passionate community of people collaborating on and contributing to its development. The resources below outline various ways you can help the world’s most popular open source web platform, regardless of your technical expertise.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Get involved in testing</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Testing for issues is crucial to the development of any software. It’s also a meaningful way for anyone to contribute. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Your help testing the WordPress 7.2 RC1 version is key to ensuring that the final release is the best it can be. While testing the upgrade process is essential, trying out new features is equally important. This <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/test/2026/10/20/help-test-wordpress-7-2/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">detailed guide</a> will walk you through testing features in WordPress 7.2.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Update your theme or plugin</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For plugin and theme authors, your products play an integral role in extending the functionality and value of WordPress for all users.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thanks for continuing to test your themes and plugins with the WordPress 7.2 beta releases. With RC1, you’ll want to conclude your testing and update the <em>“Tested up to”</em> version in your <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/plugins/wordpress-org/how-your-readme-txt-works/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">plugin’s readme file</a> to 7.2.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you find compatibility issues, please post detailed information to the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/support/forum/alphabeta/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">support forum</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Test on your hosting platforms</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Web hosts provide vital infrastructure for supporting WordPress and its users. Testing on hosting systems helps inform the development process while ensuring that WordPress and hosting platforms are fully compatible, free of errors, optimized for the best possible user experience, and that updates roll out to customer sites without issue.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Want to test WordPress on your hosting system? <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/hosting/test-results-getting-started/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Get started with configuring distributed hosting tests here</a>. Thank you to all <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/hosting/test-results/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">web hosts who help test WordPress</a>!</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Curious about testing releases in general? Follow along with the <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/test/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">testing initiatives in Make Core</a> and join the <a href=\"https://wordpress.slack.com/messages/core-test/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">#core-test channel</a> on <a href=\"https://wordpress.slack.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Making WordPress Slack</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">An RC1 haiku</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>The final bugs fall</em><br><em>Release candidate takes flight</em><br><em>Launch day draws nearer</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-right wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Props to <a href=\'https://profiles.wordpress.org/audrasjb/\' class=\'mention\'><span class=\'mentions-prefix\'>@</span>audrasjb</a>, <a href=\'https://profiles.wordpress.org/r1k0/\' class=\'mention\'><span class=\'mentions-prefix\'>@</span>r1k0</a>, and <a href=\'https://profiles.wordpress.org/courane01/\' class=\'mention\'><span class=\'mentions-prefix\'>@</span>courane01</a> for collaboration and review.</em></p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:30:\"com-wordpress:feed-additions:1\";a:1:{s:7:\"post-id\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5:\"22019\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:1;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:58:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:4:{s:0:\"\";a:7:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:37:\"Copy Your WordPress Site with Reprint\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:53:\"https://wordpress.org/news/2026/11/reprint-your-site/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:11:\"Development\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:35:\"https://wordpress.org/news/?p=22001\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:359:\"Reprint is a free, open-source, PHP-based tool that copies a WordPress site’s files and database. The plugin is available in the WordPress.org Plugin Directory, along with the command-line client used to copy the site. WordPress has long let you export your posts and pages. Moving the site itself means bringing along its theme, plugins, uploads, [&#8230;]\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:9:\"enclosure\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:3:{s:3:\"url\";s:52:\"https://videos.files.wordpress.com/KvhaIGjZ/pull.mp4\";s:6:\"length\";s:6:\"625628\";s:4:\"type\";s:9:\"video/mp4\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:15:\"Adam Zieliński\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5673:\"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Reprint is a free, open-source, PHP-based tool that copies a WordPress site’s files and database. The plugin is available in the <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/reprint/\">WordPress.org Plugin Directory</a>, along with the command-line client used to copy the site.</p>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-post-featured-image\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=2560%2C1440&#038;ssl=1\" class=\"attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" style=\"object-fit:cover;\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?w=2560&amp;ssl=1 2560w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=300%2C169&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=1024%2C576&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=768%2C432&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=1536%2C864&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/reprint-hero-scaled.png?resize=2048%2C1152&amp;ssl=1 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" /></figure>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress has long let you <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/documentation/article/tools-export-screen/\">export your posts and pages</a>. Moving the site itself means bringing along its theme, plugins, uploads, and settings, too. Making that easier has been part of <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/core/2024/06/21/data-liberation-and-wordpress-migrations/\">WordPress’s Data Liberation work</a> since 2024.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Example use cases</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can use Reprint to copy your site to a new host, or to create a local copy meant for testing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While moving your site to a new host, visitors can keep using the original. Use Reprint to copy the site, and then open the copy to check that your pages load, your images appear, and your forms work before you send visitors there. When you’re ready to switch, pause changes on the original site, make one last copy, and point your domain to the new host. The <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/reprint/guides/move-to-another-host/\">step-by-step guide to moving your site</a> walks you through the move.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can also use Reprint to create a site copy meant for testing, a place to try changes without affecting the site your visitors use. <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/reprint/getting-started/copy-a-site/\">Copy your site to your computer</a> or try the <a href=\"https://playground.wordpress.net/?clone-site=https%3A%2F%2Freprint-demo.wordpress.net\">experimental, browser-based option in WordPress Playground</a>. Use the copy to try a new layout with your existing pages, see how a plugin fits into your site, or check that everything still works after a WordPress update.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How Reprint copies a site</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Reprint sends your files and database directly to the computer or server you choose, one piece at a time, without needing to connect to an external service. The transfer can begin without your old host having to make room for an archive of the whole site.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If the connection drops during the copy, you can resume from the last saved point. If you give Reprint a new site address, it can update links that point to the old one. It builds on the <a href=\"https://make.wordpress.org/core/2025/11/27/wordpress-importer-can-now-migrate-urls-in-your-content/\">WordPress Importer’s approach to rewriting links</a> and applies it to the copied database, including links stored in site settings, blocks, shortcodes, and complex data structures like serialized data or custom fields safely without corrupting tables.</p>\n\n\n\n		<figure class=\"wp-block-jetpack-videopress jetpack-videopress-player\" style=\"\" >\n			<div class=\"jetpack-videopress-player__wrapper\"> <iframe title=\"VideoPress Video Player\" aria-label=\"VideoPress Video Player\" width=\"500\" height=\"293\" src=\"https://videopress.com/embed/KvhaIGjZ?cover=1&amp;autoPlay=1&amp;controls=0&amp;loop=1&amp;muted=1&amp;persistVolume=0&amp;playsinline=1&amp;preloadContent=metadata&amp;useAverageColor=1&amp;hd=0\" frameborder=\"0\" allowfullscreen data-resize-to-parent=\"true\" allow=\"clipboard-write; presentation\"></iframe><script src=\'https://v0.wordpress.com/js/next/videopress-iframe.js?m=1790791280\'></script></div>\n			\n			\n		</figure>\n		\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When copying a site repeatedly, Reprint figures out what changed since the last time and copies only the files it needs.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Try Reprint</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You don’t need to connect your own site to see how Reprint works. Try the <a href=\"https://playground.wordpress.net/?clone-site=https%3A%2F%2Freprint-demo.wordpress.net\">experimental, browser-based option in WordPress Playground</a>. You can copy a sample site right in your browser, with nothing to install.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you’re ready to work with your own pages and settings, start with a test site you manage. The <a href=\"https://developer.wordpress.org/reprint/getting-started/copy-a-site/\">guide to making your first copy</a> takes you from installing the plugin to opening the copied site on your computer.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:30:\"com-wordpress:feed-additions:1\";a:1:{s:7:\"post-id\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5:\"22001\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:2;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:4:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:38:\"WordCamp Asia 2027 Is Coming to Penang\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:55:\"https://wordpress.org/news/2026/11/wc-asia-2027-penang/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:9:\"Community\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:6:\"Events\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:35:\"https://wordpress.org/news/?p=21919\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:344:\"Next year, WordCamp Asia 2027 heads to Penang, Malaysia. From April 9 to 11, the WordPress community will gather at the Penang Waterfront Convention Centre for three days of contribution, learning, and connection. Tickets are on sale and sponsorship applications are open, so now is the time to make your plans. In 2026, WordCamp Asia [&#8230;]\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:17:\"Nicholas Garofalo\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:81524:\"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Next year, WordCamp Asia 2027 heads to Penang, Malaysia. From April 9 to 11, the WordPress community will gather at the Penang Waterfront Convention Centre for three days of contribution, learning, and connection. Tickets are on sale and sponsorship applications are open, so now is the time to make your plans.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-82d461e8 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"https://asia.wordcamp.org/2027/tickets/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(42,5,123) 0%,rgb(42,5,123) 100%)\" target=\"_blank\">Get Your Event Pass</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"https://asia.wordcamp.org/2027/call-for-sponsors/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(42,5,123) 0%,rgb(42,5,123) 100%)\" target=\"_blank\">Become a Sponsor</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-background wp-element-button\" href=\"https://asia.wordcamp.org/2027/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgb(42,5,123) 0%,rgb(42,5,123) 100%)\" target=\"_blank\">About WordCamp Asia</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In 2026, <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/news/2026/04/celebrating-wcasia-2026/\">WordCamp Asia</a> brought 2,627 attendees to Mumbai, India. More than 1,500 participants joined Contributor Day, where table leads guided work on more than 20 contribution tables. The conference days that followed covered topics ranging from AI and developer workflows to enterprise WordPress and journalism on the open web, and closed with a panel featuring WordPress Executive Director <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/4thhubbard/\">Mary Hubbard</a>, <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/peterwilsoncc/\">Peter Wilson</a>, and <a href=\"https://profiles.wordpress.org/sergeybiryukov/\">Sergey Biryukov</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">WordPress is not a company. It is a shared commitment to keeping the web open.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Mary Hubbard, Executive Director, WordPress</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The mix of hands-on work and big-picture conversation is what sets a WordCamp apart. You learn from the people who build, scale, and maintain WordPress every day, trade ideas in the hallway between sessions, and head home with new collaborators and fresh energy for the work ahead.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Penang offers a memorable setting for WC Asia. George Town, a short drive from the venue, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and National Geographic named Penang one of the best places in the world to travel to in 2027. The island is famous for its food, from internationally-recognized street food to fine dining, and it is one of Malaysia’s leading destinations for tourism. If you can, give yourself a day or two on either side of the conference to explore.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure data-wp-context=\"{&quot;galleryId&quot;:&quot;6afd1f5913b37&quot;}\" data-wp-interactive=\"core/gallery\" class=\"wp-block-gallery alignfull has-nested-images columns-8 is-cropped has-black-background-color has-background wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-container-core-gallery-is-layout-db4b8a9e wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\" style=\"border-width:20px;border-radius:2px\">\n<figure data-wp-context=\"{&quot;imageId&quot;:&quot;6afd1f59142cd&quot;}\" data-wp-interactive=\"core/image\" data-wp-key=\"6afd1f59142cd\" class=\"wp-block-image size-large wp-lightbox-container\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"684\" data-wp-class--hide=\"state.isContentHidden\" data-wp-class--show=\"state.isContentVisible\" data-wp-init=\"callbacks.setButtonStyles\" data-wp-on--click=\"actions.showLightbox\" data-wp-on--load=\"callbacks.setButtonStyles\" data-wp-on--pointerdown=\"actions.preloadImage\" data-wp-on--pointerenter=\"actions.preloadImageWithDelay\" data-wp-on--pointerleave=\"actions.cancelPreload\" data-wp-on-window--resize=\"callbacks.setButtonStyles\" data-id=\"21983\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-21983\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/34544681862_e804672e3e_k.jpg?resize=1024%2C684&#038;ssl=1\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/34544681862_e804672e3e_k.jpg?resize=1024%2C684&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/wordpress.org/news/files/2026/11/34544681862_e804672e3e_k.jpg?resize=300%2C200